From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 14:33:21 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09837/11362] [outer-loop] Demote and repair
 verification_commands; file the red suite

Operator directive: demote and repair, do not delete.

DEMOTE. The repository-wide suite is out of the pre-launch precondition
set in both flagship shard modules. A precondition exists to prove the
resources a run needs are present; repo-wide suite health is not one,
and gating a live model load on it blocked the run for a reason
unrelated to the measurement. The set is now six focused commands, all
of which already exited 0 in both blocked artifacts, at about 25s
against the 900-2400s the full suite consumed.

REPAIR. The inline expression became focused_verification_ok(), a named
function in a tested seam -- the old check lived inside a
pragma-no-cover function and was never under test. It fails closed: an
empty set is False, and a row with no exit_code is False. The repo's
opposite pattern (experiment_6457:1246, exit_code in (0, None)) treats
never-ran as a pass and is not copied.

Blast radius was one decision point, not two: exp6582 imports exp6581
as shared and delegates _collect_preconditions.

Spec: REQ-REPORT-6581-VERIFY-SCOPE and
SCENARIO-REPORT-6581-VERIFY-FAIL-CLOSED added.
REQ-REPORT-6582-VERIFICATION-BUDGET, which mandated the full suite at a
4801s timeout, is superseded in place with its text preserved and its
still-valid second and third sentences kept in force.

Mutation proofs, each applied then restored: removing the empty-set
guard goes RED; the fail-open (0, None) variant goes RED; re-adding the
full suite goes RED in both modules. Restored GREEN, 26 passed, 100%
coverage on both modules, ruff and spec coverage clean.

COST, stated rather than hidden: this removes the last reporter of the
red suite (87/68/470/433 failures over twelve days). Nothing else runs
it -- research_conductor.run_tests has a correct full=True branch but
every call site passes full=False. The signal is filed in
ops/known-issues.md with the measurements, the coverage/xdist caveat,
and three ordered steps toward a real home.

Not touched: idle_supported_gpu, which correctly detected a busy GPU;
and the retirement state of either experiment.

